  "content": [
    {
      "id": "summary-01",
      "kind": "summary",
      "text": "The team aligned on a bounded Northstar evaluation: 10 locations first, with expansion tied to repeat operational use rather than initial sign-ins. Maya will confirm the first-location list by September 4, and Jules will publish the adoption dashboard by September 11.",
      "sequence": 0,
      "language": "en",
      "origin": "source_ai",
      "source_external_id": "demo-summary-001"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-01",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "Thanks for joining. I want to leave with customer-safe language for Northstar and a way to tell whether the evaluation is actually working.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "maya-chen",
      "sequence": 1,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:00:12.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:00:29.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 12000,
      "end_offset_ms": 29000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-01"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-02",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "They are excited. If we can tell them all 28 locations are in scope from day one, I think we keep the momentum and make the September story much easier.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "rob-ellis",
      "sequence": 2,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:00:31.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:00:49.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 31000,
      "end_offset_ms": 49000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-02"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-03",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "I would separate excitement from evidence. Initial logins can come from training or curiosity. They do not tell us that managers are using the workflow week after week without someone correcting it manually.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "jules-martin",
      "sequence": 3,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:00:52.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:01:18.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 52000,
      "end_offset_ms": 78000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-03"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-04",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "What would count as enough evidence? We need a threshold I can explain without turning this into an analytics lecture.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "maya-chen",
      "sequence": 4,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:01:21.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:01:35.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 81000,
      "end_offset_ms": 95000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-04"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-05",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "For a first cohort of 10 locations, I would look for at least 8 to complete the weekly workflow four weeks in a row. The completion needs to happen without manual correction by our implementation team.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "jules-martin",
      "sequence": 5,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:01:38.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:02:04.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 98000,
      "end_offset_ms": 124000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-05"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-06",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "Eight out of 10 for four consecutive weeks is more conservative than I hoped. Is there a reason not to treat the first two weeks as a signal and begin expanding while we measure the rest?",
      "speaker_participant_id": "rob-ellis",
      "sequence": 6,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:02:08.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:02:26.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 128000,
      "end_offset_ms": 146000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-06"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-07",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "Because a rushed expansion would convert an unproven pattern into a broader operating commitment. The first cohort is how we learn whether the product holds up in the places that have to use it every week.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "anika-patel",
      "sequence": 7,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:02:29.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:02:51.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 149000,
      "end_offset_ms": 171000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-07"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-08",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "Could we call the first 10 a launch and leave the rest as a follow-on phase? That still gives Northstar a simple message.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "rob-ellis",
      "sequence": 8,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:02:54.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:03:07.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 174000,
      "end_offset_ms": 187000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-08"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-09",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "No. We should call it an evaluation with a defined first cohort. I am setting the scope at 10 locations. We expand only after at least 8 of those 10 have completed four consecutive weekly workflows without manual correction. That is the line we should hold.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "anika-patel",
      "sequence": 9,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:03:10.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:03:42.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 190000,
      "end_offset_ms": 222000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-09",
      "metadata": {
        "evidence_role": "definitive"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-10",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "That works. I will confirm which 10 locations are in the first cohort with Northstar and bring the list back by September 4. I will not position the other 18 as committed scope.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "maya-chen",
      "sequence": 10,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:03:46.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:04:08.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 226000,
      "end_offset_ms": 248000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-10"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-11",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "I will publish the dashboard by September 11. It will show the weekly workflow completion rate by location, the consecutive-week count, and every manual correction so the threshold is auditable.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "jules-martin",
      "sequence": 11,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:04:12.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:04:33.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 252000,
      "end_offset_ms": 273000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-11"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-12",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "Please make the dashboard readable by Customer Success too. If the number is close, we will need to understand whether one location is blocked by training or whether the workflow itself is failing.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "maya-chen",
      "sequence": 12,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:04:36.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:04:57.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 276000,
      "end_offset_ms": 297000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-12"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-13",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "I can add a short annotation field for that. I will keep the underlying measure unchanged so we do not explain away misses after the fact.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "jules-martin",
      "sequence": 13,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:05:01.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:05:16.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 301000,
      "end_offset_ms": 316000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-13"
    },
    {
      "id": "transcript-14",
      "kind": "transcript",
      "text": "Good. Rob, please use the evaluation language in the next customer conversation. Maya and Jules have the two follow-ups; we will revisit expansion only when the evidence is in.",
      "speaker_participant_id": "anika-patel",
      "sequence": 14,
      "started_at": "2026-08-24T16:05:20.000Z",
      "ended_at": "2026-08-24T16:05:39.000Z",
      "start_offset_ms": 320000,
      "end_offset_ms": 339000,
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "origin": "imported",
      "source_external_id": "demo-turn-001-14"
    }
  ],
